      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.29,
          "end": 4.97,
          "en": "So let's now add our first component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.97,
          "end": 8.42,
          "en": "because this is just our main Vue app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.42,
          "end": 11.9,
          "en": "But I mentioned before in the component introduction module,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11.9,
          "end": 14.18,
          "en": "that in Vue you have both.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 14.18,
          "end": 18.24,
          "en": "You have Vue apps and you have Vue components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 18.24,
          "end": 22.58,
          "en": "And every component is like a mini app where you just have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 22.58,
          "end": 25.29,
          "en": "the possibility of combining multiple components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 25.29,
          "end": 28.94,
          "en": "into one app and where eventually covered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 28.94,
          "end": 30.37,
          "en": "in the next module.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 30.37,
          "end": 31.53,
          "en": "Those mini apps,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 31.53,
          "end": 34.75,
          "en": "those components will also be able to talk to each other",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 34.75,
          "end": 38.27,
          "en": "and you'll be able to build complex user interfaces",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 38.27,
          "end": 41.82,
          "en": "by combining different components together.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 41.82,
          "end": 45.27,
          "en": "Now, it is a convention that you create a new folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 45.27,
          "end": 48.26,
          "en": "and you fold another file named components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 48.26,
          "end": 51.683,
          "en": "and your source folder to hold your components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 53.54,
          "end": 57.25,
          "en": "Simply just to make it clear that these are now components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 57.25,
          "end": 59.423,
          "en": "and not just any Vue app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 60.43,
          "end": 61.263,
          "en": "Now in here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 61.263,
          "end": 66.263,
          "en": "I'm going to add my new FriendContact.vue file to hold",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 66.36,
          "end": 68.18,
          "en": "the friend-contact component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 68.18,
          "end": 69.48,
          "en": "which I want to create.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
